::SPEECH_U06_L02_Quiz_Q01::
Question ID: SPEECH_U06_L02_Quiz_Q01
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.08
Question:
Interview and discussion item 1: Which choice best supports professional conversation?
{
~A. Give a vague answer with no example#This choice is incomplete because it does not match the professional purpose, audience, or communication setting.
~B. Interrupt instead of listening#This choice may sound related, but it does not fully support respectful professional communication or discussion skill.
=C. Answer directly and include a specific relevant example#Correct. This choice supports professional communication by matching purpose, audience, tone, listening, and collaboration expectations.
~D. Disagree without explaining a reason#This choice weakens communication because it ignores how the listener or group will understand the message.
}
::SPEECH_U06_L02_Quiz_Q02::
Question ID: SPEECH_U06_L02_Quiz_Q02
MLA Standard: MLA.SPEECH.COM.09
Question:
Interview and discussion item 2: Which choice best supports professional conversation?
{
=A. Build on another speaker idea with a useful suggestion#Correct. This choice supports professional communication by matching purpose, audience, tone, listening, and collaboration expectations.
~B. Interrupt instead of listening#This choice may sound related, but it does not fully support respectful professional communication or discussion skill.
~C. Ignore the previous speaker comment#This choice reflects a misconception. Recheck audience, tone, listening, or collaboration expectations.
~D. Disagree without explaining a reason#This choice weakens communication because it ignores how the listener or group will understand the message.
}
